## Why This Is Asked
Dynamic connectivity with insertions and deletions is a classic hard problem. This offline approach tests understanding of edge lifetimes and versioning, and how to combine segment trees with DSU rollback for log-scale updates.

## Key Concepts
- DSU with rollback (no path compression) to enable undo.
- Segment tree over time to map edge active intervals to time ranges.
- Offline processing: traverse tree, apply unions, answer leaf queries, then rollback.

## Code Example
```javascript
class RollbackDSU {
  constructor(n){
    this.parent = Array.from({length:n}, (_,i)=>i);
    this.sz = Array(n).fill(1);
    this.ch = [];
  }
  find(x){ while (this.parent[x]!==x) x = this.parent[x]; return x; }
  union(a,b){
    a = this.find(a); b = this.find(b);
    if (a===b){ this.ch.push(null); return; }
    if (this.sz[a] < this.sz[b]) [a,b] = [b,a];
    this.ch.push([b, this.parent[b], a, this.sz[a]]);
    this.parent[b] = a; this.sz[a] += this.sz[b];
  }
  snapshot(){ return this.ch.length; }
  rollback(snap){
    while (this.ch.length > snap){
      const ch = this.ch.pop();
      if (!ch) continue;
      const [b, oldP, a, oldS] = ch;
      this.parent[b] = oldP; this.sz[a] = oldS;
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to combine Trie augmentation with order-statistics across prefixes, handling duplicates and dynamic updates. Probes memory usage and worst-case behavior.

## Key Concepts

- Trie augmentation with subtree weight sums per prefix node
- Per-node multisets supporting duplicates and kth-largest queries
- Efficient updates along root-to-leaf paths with delta propagation
- Trade-offs: memory overhead vs query/update speed

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(){
    this.next = new Map();
    this.subtreeSum = 0;
    this.weights = new Map(); // weight -> count
  }
}

function addToMultiset(ms, w, delta){
  ms.set(w, (ms.get(w) || 0) + delta);
  if (ms.get(w) <= 0) ms.delete(w);
}

function insert(root, s, w){
  let cur = root;
  addToMultiset(cur.weights, w, 1);
  cur.subtreeSum += w;
  for (let ch of s){
    if (!cur.next.has(ch)) cur.next.set(ch, new Node());
    cur = cur.next.get(ch);
    addToMultiset(cur.weights, w, 1);
    cur.subtreeSum += w;
  }
}

function erase(root, s, w){
  let cur = root;
  addToMultiset(cur.weights, w, -1);
  cur.subtreeSum -= w;
  for (let ch of s){
    cur = cur.next.get(ch);
    addToMultiset(cur.weights, w, -1);
    cur.subtreeSum -= w;
  }
}
```

